# LAN Caddyfile example
#
# Caddy natively supports h2c reverse-proxying with the h2c:// scheme.
# No extra module is needed.
#
# A LAN-only host is usually not reachable from the internet, so Let's Encrypt
# HTTP-01 fails. Default to Caddy's internal CA and trust its root CA on the
# Synology (DSM Control Panel > Security > Certificate) so azath client can
# verify TLS. For a real public cert, switch to DNS-01 via Cloudflare and the
# caddy-dns/cloudflare plugin.

azath-lan.example {
	reverse_proxy h2c://127.0.0.1:7800

	tls internal
}